usage: flair align [-h] -r READS [READS ...] (-g GENOME | --mm_index MM_INDEX)
                   [-o OUTPUT] [-t THREADS] [--junction_bed JUNCTION_BED]
                   [--native_rna] [--quality QUALITY]
                   [--filter_type {keepsup,removesup,separate}]
                   [--min_fragment_size MIN_FRAGMENT_SIZE]
                   [--max_intron_len MAX_INTRON_LEN]

FLAIR align outputs an unfiltered bam file and a filtered bam file for use in
the downstream pipeline

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -g GENOME, --genome GENOME
                        FASTA of reference genome, can be minimap2 indexed
  --mm_index MM_INDEX   minimap2 index .mmi file
  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT
                        output file name base (default: flair.aligned)
  -t THREADS, --threads THREADS
                        minimap2 number of threads (default: 4)
  --junction_bed JUNCTION_BED
                        annotated isoforms/junctions bed file for splice site-
                        guided minimap2 genomic alignment
  --native_rna          use native-RNA specific alignment parameters for
                        minimap2
  --quality QUALITY     minimum MAPQ of read alignment to the genome (default:
                        0)
  --filter_type {keepsup,removesup,separate}
                        method of filtering chimeric alignments (potential
                        fusion reads); separate is required for downstream
                        work with fusions, keepsup keeps supplementary
                        alignments for isoform detection and does not allow
                        gene fusion detection (default: removesup)
  --min_fragment_size MIN_FRAGMENT_SIZE
                        minimum size of alignment kept, used in minimap -s.
                        More important when doing downstream fusion detection
                        (default: 80)
  --max_intron_len MAX_INTRON_LEN
                        maximum intron length in genomic alignment. Longer can
                        help recover more novel isoforms with long introns
                        (default: 200k)

required named arguments:
  -r READS [READS ...], --reads READS [READS ...]
                        FASTA/FASTQ file(s) of raw reads, either space or
                        comma separated
